  "body": "Accept an explicit zero taper when a script or MCP client adds or edits a Wire Contour. The patch validator reads the typed operation value when the saved form omits its default. Other operation kinds and unknown fields retain their existing checks.\n\nThe regression test wire_contour_accepts_an_explicit_zero_taper_on_add_and_edit creates a vertical operation, sets a taper and clears it. It also checks a misspelled field and a field on the wrong operation kind.\n\nBefore the fixture refresh, the quick gate passed all 16 steps and 373 tests. Strict clippy passed on all camcraft-app targets. The normal CLI produced the same 331-byte vertical program for an omitted taper, zero, 0.0 and an edit from 3 degrees to zero. The 3 degree control produced 496 bytes. A misspelled field, a wire taper on a Face operation, and a string value each failed without an NC file. Verification used the offline software only.\n\nThe current head is 79b4d4339. It includes the upstream Apple silicon release fixture from #2934 through a clean merge. The full quick gate passed 17/17 steps in 19.4 minutes on that head. The optimized pocket3d_hsm bore test now passes with 3158 moves, 3130 planar moves and 1141 arcs. The complete reached heavy gate passed all 199 steps in 57.8 minutes on macOS arm64.\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: A Wire Contour accepts an explicit zero taper on creation and when an edit returns it to a vertical cut.\n\nFixes #2925\n\n\n",
